<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2890" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antĭpŏlis</span></b> , is,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀντίπολις</span>.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city in Gaul</i>, now <i>Antibes</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 4, 5, § 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2,
			5</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antĭpŏlĭtānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>from Antipolis</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thynni,</span>”
				<i>found in that region</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					13, 103</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 4, 89</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An old settlement in Latium</i>, <i>afterwards Janiculum</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				9, § 68</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
